{
  "about": "Cards sent between decks and in and out of a sideboard (src/collection/binderFlows.ts sendDeckCard, toSideboard, toMain; the Android app's data/BinderFlows.kt). No copy is made or lost: All cards' real copies are the same after, less 'added' (a deck that holds none of its cards sending a card to a binder adds it, as from search), and the binder views and No binder add up to them. Into a deck that holds its cards (Physical or Proxy) a move takes the real copies with their binders and spots; a copy, or what a move doesn't bring, comes out of No binder (Physical only) and the rest is to pull (proxies). A sideboard, a Considering list or a deck that doesn't hold its cards only lists the card; a move's real copies go back to their binders, the rest to No binder. Run by tests/collection/moveFlows.test.ts and the Android app's MoveFlowsTest.kt. Shapes as in returnToBinderVectors.json, with several 'decks' (each may have 'sideboard' and 'considering': [{ id, qty }]). 'do': send { from, card, qty, to: { deck, part: main|sideboard|considering } | { binder }, keep } (keep: a copy), toSideboard { deck, card }, toMain { deck, card }. expect.collections: every collection but wishlists; expect.decks: each deck after (sideboard / considering checked when given); expect.sent: what sendDeckCard said it did.",
